WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.020
Hi, this is

2
00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:12.500
Mitchell. So I will be presenting my final
software prototype,

3
00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:17.440
which is AmaiReady. So "Amai" is a Shona
word for mother, but it also

4
00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:22.380
sounds like "Am I". And that's very
intentional, because AmaiReady is

5
00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:27.440
a maternal delivery preparation and
support system designed for pregnant

6
00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:31.120
women living in rural communities in
Zimbabwe.

7
00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:33.620
So what exactly is the problem?

8
00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:39.860
Many pregnant women struggle to prepare
all the supplies that they need

9
00:00:39.860 --> 00:00:45.340
for delivery. Some are asked to source
maternity kit items themselves.

10
00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:50.440
This includes gloves, cotton wool and
maternity pads.

11
00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:55.420
And additionally, access to clinics may
also be affected by distance,

12
00:00:55.420 --> 00:00:59.920
cost and limited information. So mothers
may not know what items are

13
00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:04.120
still missing, which clinic is the nearest
to them, or where to request

14
00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:07.260
for help. So why exactly is this a
problem?

15
00:01:07.940 --> 00:01:11.440
Missing supplies delay delivery
preparation.

16
00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:15.500
So this means that mothers would only
discover missing items close to

17
00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:19.760
their delivery date. Information is often
then scattered between clinic

18
00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:23.760
visits, paper records, sometimes even
verbal instructions.

19
00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:30.320
And support administrators may also
struggle to track requests consistently.

20
00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:35.720
So this then creates stress during a
period that is already vulnerable

21
00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:41.560
for pregnant women. So this is the problem
that AmaiReady aims to solve.

22
00:01:41.980 --> 00:01:46.180
So AmaiReady brings the main preparation
tasks into one system.

23
00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:51.680
This is where now you will see a mother
can register, log in and create

24
00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:55.040
her pregnancy profile, make requests, and
so forth.

25
00:01:55.660 --> 00:01:59.040
And on the other hand, the administrator
can log in securely, review

26
00:01:59.040 --> 00:01:59.880
the support requests...
